@@ -2877,6 +2877,10 @@ Changes thanks to claude sonnet 4.5 and chatgpt 5, in `CvCityAI::AI_permanentSpe
 
 I have noticed AI goes for great general leader, when it is much better to go for a military instructor that would scale throughout the game, and in top hammer cities, especially if they have heroic epic. Plus removed the military instructor per city limit. Results ingame are very good.
 
+Update: BBAI save-file 450 testing showed a remaining edge case: France had a Great General in Orleans at T132, `AI_join` rejected Orleans as `city-not-safe` and rejected Lyons/Rheims as `no-safe-path`, then the plot-danger branch attached the Great General to a low-value Longbowman (`baseCombat=4`, `xp=4`, `healing=0`).
+
+Great General unit-attachment branches now use tunable minimum target gates that default very high, so Great Generals effectively keep preferring Military Academy or Military Instructor unless these thresholds are deliberately lowered. In the latest T200 retest, France's low-value Longbowman attachment was rejected from T132 to T136 and the Great General joined Orleans at T137; the same gate also rejected a United States Longbowman from T186 to T188, and that Great General joined Washington at T189.
+
 ## 70 - (Seemingly fixed) Base advciv bug of forcing an artist specialist even if it is invalid and then firing a failed assert, in CvCityAI::AI_assignWorkingPlots
 
 See code comments i.e. in `CvCityAI::AI_assignWorkingPlots` there for details, seemingly now fixed with the help of chatgpt 5 and my prompts or such, check if accurate.

diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index 1523cccbe..53e6d7d9f 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@ Some features are not supported in AdvCiv-SAS; e.g., non-English languages, pre-
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6022+) **SAS game-summary log:** added a separate `SASGameSummary_*.log` for compact autoplay and AI-strength review. It records high-level run context such as economy, expansion, city and battle history, worked plots, diplomacy, unit composition, game state, and in-game bonus appearances/disappearances, complementing BBAI logs by summarizing what happened before or alongside detailed AI-decision traces. Note: it currently contains spoilers: a spoiler-free implementation was considered, so the human/active player can give to an LLM or such their play summary and get LLM or such suggestions or feedback/analysis, but it would require an extensive rework, so currently this is not supported; therefore, SAS game-summary log should as of now not be treated as a spoiler-free player-advice export. Note 2: depending on `SAS_GAME_SUMMARY_TURN_INTERVAL` value, the last turn may not appear in the log: for example, an autoplay run of 200 turns ends at T200 and thus does not seem to show the T200 data, only up to T190, so autoplay at least 201 turns to show T200 for example if you have this issue. See also [README.md (DLL Logging)](/README.md#dll-logging).
 - **BBAI worker log split:** added separate worker and Work Boat / `UNITAI_WORKER_SEA` BBAI log-level defines so ordinary `SAS_BBAI_UNIT_LOG_LEVEL` can focus on non-worker unit behavior such as scrapping, army movement, and combat-unit decisions. Worker and worker-sea logs had become noisy enough to hide those unit decisions, and Work Boats use distinct logic from land workers, so they now have their own category as well.
 - **BBAI Settler log split:** added `SAS_BBAI_SETTLER_LOG_LEVEL`, separated from UNIT so Settlers and other units can be inspected independently. This notably covers city-site decisions, Settler movement, scouting, returns, founding, (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6027+) parking reasons, danger context, and city escort pools; FOUND as of now separately controls detailed city-site scoring calculations. This notably lets UNIT investigate other unit behavior without enabling the multi-megabyte first-city Settler traces needed for example for the Berlin, Karakorum, and Cuzco regression tests.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6031+) **Great General BBAI diagnostics:** added `SAS_BBAI_GREAT_GENERAL_LOG_LEVEL`, separated from UNIT notably so Military Academy construction, Military Instructor joining, Warlord attachment, target-city choice, and target-unit choice can be inspected together without enabling broad unit logs. This notably helped isolate a bad France sample where `AI_join` rejected all cities for safety/path reasons, then the plot-danger branch attached a Great General to a low-value Longbowman.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6031+) **Great General BBAI diagnostics:** added `SAS_BBAI_GREAT_GENERAL_LOG_LEVEL`, separated from UNIT notably so Military Academy construction, Military Instructor joining, Great General unit attachment, target-city choice, and target-unit choice can be inspected together without enabling broad unit logs. This notably helped isolate a bad France sample where `AI_join` rejected all cities for safety/path reasons, then the plot-danger branch attached a Great General to a low-value Longbowman.
 - **Culture-victory BBAI diagnostics:** added a new dedicated `SAS_BBAI_CULTURE_LOG_LEVEL` notably for diagnosing premature, uneven, or wasteful AI culture investment without enabling broad player/city logs. It records for example culture-stage reasons, current/projected Legendary-city countdowns and rival ranking, competing victory progress, actual culture-slider decisions, per-city weights and production, and culture contributed by production processes and assigned specialists.
 - **Citizen-allocation BBAI diagnostics:** added a dedicated `SAS_BBAI_CITIZEN_LOG_LEVEL` notably for finding worked plots or specialists that the AI's full city-aware comparison would replace, but its faster preliminary selection overlooked. At the highest level, it also reports suspicious worked/unworked plot pairs under a simple food-first yield check.
 - **Evacuation and retreat BBAI diagnostics:** added `SAS_BBAI_EVACUATION_LOG_LEVEL`. It notably helps investigate evacuation/retreat behavior without broad city or unit logging, for doomed cities, workers, and naval units.
@@ -381,7 +381,8 @@ Note 2: Master–vassal(s) changes are intended to strengthen overall AI play by
 - **City-counter role pruning (e.g. Macemen)**: Removed `UNITAI_CITY_COUNTER` from **non-versatile** units (e.g., `UNIT_MACEMAN`). For example for macemen, as city defenders they’re too easy to punish—knights counter them hard, and even crossbow stacks can beat defending macemen—so they’re better assigned to **offensive** `UnitAI` roles. While macemen beat pikemen, pikes seldom assault cities efficiently, so the city-counter slot isn’t warranted. The same adjustment applies to any other units with this mismatch.
 - **Mounted "Counter" role pruning:** Removed `UNITAI_COUNTER` from the mounted units (`UNIT_CHARIOT`, `UNIT_EGYPTIAN_WAR_CHARIOT`, `UNIT_CARTHAGE_NUMIDIAN_CAVALRY`) that had it. Rationale: mounted units don’t "receive defense bonuses" (note: not related to bonuses/ressources) and can be countered by other units; assigning them to COUNTER can park them in cities (e.g. seemingly seen in autoplay with War Chariots) and occupies a slot **Longbowmen** are more fit to fill as they unlock early and are cheap and versatile defenders, so these mounted unit lines are better used for offense roles rather during its window—or skipped outside it.
 - **Stack attack order — spend expendables first:** stack attacks now prefer **bombard/collateral** and **low-effective-strength/low-XP** units first (once the stack commits to attack), preserving elite finishers. Rationale: economically efficient (older/weaker units cost upkeep but scale poorly) and strategically safer (keep high-value units for decisive blows or retreats). Change in `CvSelectionGroupAI::AI_getBestGroupAttacker`. Toggle via SAS defines for A/B testing. See [KI#89](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#89---improved-in-an-attack-stack-attack-with-lower-value-effective-strength-xp-health-units-first).
-- **Great Generals — prefer Military Instructor, focus on hammer hubs:** AI now favours settling Great Generals as **Military Instructors** over attaching them as unit leaders, as the instructor bonus scales better into the late game. **Targeting:** strong bias to the **top 3 hammer cities** with **decreasing weights** (top-1 most, then top-2/3 progressively less). Extra preference if the city **has / is building** the **Heroic Epic effect** building. **Limit removed:** cities may host **multiple** Military Instructors (no per-city cap). Implemented in `CvCityAI::AI_permanentSpecialistValue` and `CvUnitAI::AI_generalMove`. See [KI#69](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#69---tremendously-improved-ai-going-for-great-general-leaders-while-military-instructors-are-much-better-with-added-logic-to-favour-top-hammer-cities-remove-military-instructor-per-city-limit-favour-it-further-if-have-or-building-heroic-epic-effect-building-etc). Note: sometimes/rarely ignored in autoplay.
